WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.034
[Wind howling]

2
00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.916
[Whooshing]

3
00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:42.304
- [Car alarm blaring]
- [Glass shatters]

4
00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.747
%% [acoustic guitar]

5
00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:01.693
% % We'll meet again% %

6
00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:04.059
% % Don't know where% %

7
00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.690
% % Don't know when% %

8
00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:10.600
% % But I know we'll meet again% %

9
00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.003
% % Some sunny day% %

10
00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:21.239
% % Keep smiling through% %

11
00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.544
% % Just like you% %

12
00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.880
% % Always do% %

13
00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:28.386
% % Till the blue skies% %

14
00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:31.151
% % Drive the dark clouds% %

15
00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:35.786
- % % Far away% %
- [children shouting]

16
00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.888
% % And will you please say hello% %

17
00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.990
[phone ringing]

18
00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.966
Um, Dr. Dutten,

19
00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.166
- my aunt's in town.
- Mm-hmm.

20
00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.300
And she's sick, too.

21
00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.606
[Exhales forcefully]
I'm gonna need you to stay late tonight.

22
00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.544
- Oh. You are?
- You know, you should probably

23
00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.342
text your Aunt Scotty

24
00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.907
and tell him you can't make it
to the baseball game today.

25
00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.577
Wait a second.

26
00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.917
- Okay, look, Scotty and I, we're not...
- Oh, come on, Becca.

27
00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.957
- I mean...
- It's the worse-kept secret in town.

28
00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.958
Now, that is saying a lot.

29
00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.426
Go on.
Get outta here.

30
00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.758
Go have some fun.

31
00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.025
Thanks, Dr. Dutten.

32
00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:18.327
[Man on P.A. System, indistinct]

33
00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:23.099
[Crowd cheering, applauding]

34
00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.448
Well, I don't care what the calendar says.

35
00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.508
Opening day...
That's the first day of spring.

36
00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.645
No, no, no.
The sheriff never pays for coffee.

37
00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.622
Well, that's kind of you, Ben.

38
00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.817
But the principal still has to pay
his parking tickets.

39
00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.825
[Chuckles]

40
00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.555
- Start him a tab.
- Yes, sir.

41
00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.462
[Cheering continues]

42
00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.435
Kid throws fast.

43
00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.200
Just like he drives.

44
00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:57.038
Nice pitch, Scotty.

45
00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.340
[Man]
Come on, man! Come on, guys!

46
00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.849
Strike two!

47
00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:07.079
Whoo! Yeah!

48
00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.793
Center field.

49
00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.366
Oh, Jesus Christ.

50
00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.136
[Man]
Hey, Tommy!

51
00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.247
- Stay there.
- What's he doing?

52
00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.873
- Boys, get in the dugout.
- Move it off.

53
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.577
- Get off!
- Bring it in. Bring it in.

54
00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.778
- Get them off the field.
- [Man shouting]

55
00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.377
Get them in the dugout, Principal.

56
00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.946
Rory. Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa.

57
00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.959
Hey, Rory, we got
a ballgame going on here.

58
00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.291
We're playing ball,
and you come out with a gun?

59
00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:53.389
What the hell are you doing?

60
00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.229
Aw, Ror.

61
00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.769
You're drunk, that's all.

62
00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.533
All right? Let's just lay the gun down.

63
00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.610
Rory, lay the gun down.

64
00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.306
Hmm? Lay it down.

65
00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.082
Hell, Rory, come on.
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa.

66
00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.483
Rory?

67
00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.146
[Crowd murmuring]

68
00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:20.019
Now, you lay that gun down.

69
00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:25.994
Rory?

70
00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.667
[Crowd gasping]

71
00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.670
Oh, my God.

72
00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.168
[Chattering]

73
00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.885
[Radio chatter]

74
00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:09.167
[Man]
I'll have blood alcohol for you in the morning.

75
00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.869
[Door opens]

76
00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.877
A full tox screen will take about a week.

77
00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.175
[Door closes]

78
00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.148
How are you holding up, David?

79
00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.182
Peggy here yet?

80
00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:23.245
She just walked in with her boy.

81
00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.686
David, perhaps now is not the best time.

82
00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:33.956
Son, settle down.

83
00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.959
- Hey, Curt.
- [Stifled whimper]

84
00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:41.197
Uh...

85
00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:43.139
I'm so sorry.

86
00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.308
I liked Rory. I liked him a lot.

87
00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.177
What was he doing out there?

88
00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.216
He had been drinking, that's all.

89
00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.718
Rory quit two years ago.

90
00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.880
You know how proud he was of that.

91
00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.789
Is that what you're saying,
that he was drunk?

92
00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.225
- Is that what you're telling people?
- No.

93
00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:05.696
That you had to do it...
had to shoot the town drunk.

94
00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:23.206
[Scraping in distance]

95
00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.552
[Scraping continues]

96
00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:41.587
You did the right thing.

97
00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.193
I need a new blade for this.

98
00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.733
Hey, David.

99
00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:53.236
You did the right thing.

100
00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:08.283
You should be sleeping.

101
00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:17.961
[Phone ringing]

102
00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.964
[Man]
Sheriff's Department.

103
00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:21.624
No, ma'am,
we can't comment on that.

104
00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:24.465
That's an ongoing investigation.

105
00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:27.529
No, ma'am, the sheriff
is not here right now,

106
00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:30.542
but I can see if the deputy will...

107
00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:34.205
- Amateur.
- [Phone ringing]

108
00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.772
Sheriff's Department.
Mm-hmm.

109
00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.479
That's the medical examiner on line two.

110
00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:47.058
Morning, Jim.
What have we got?

111
00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:50.061
The toxicology reports are in.
The results are negative.

112
00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:51.721
- Come again?
- There was no alcohol...

113
00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:54.231
No, I heard what you said,
Jim, but that's not right.

114
00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.827
- Rory was...
- David, we did the test twice.

115
00:08:57.904 --> 00:09:00.600
Rory wasn't drunk.
There was no alcohol in his bloodstream.

116
00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:03.801
We'll get the drug results
back in a couple of days, maybe a week.

117
00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:05.639
Yeah, okay.

118
00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:07.679
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

119
00:09:07.747 --> 00:09:09.806
[Man on police radio]
Do you want this car...

120
00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:13.814
[Man #2 on radio]
Bring it down here.

121
00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:40.100
Ben?

122
00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:43.106
Ben!

123
00:09:47.219 --> 00:09:49.084
Hey.

124
00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:54.818
- Hey, Ben. Ben!
- [Snapping fingers]

125
00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:57.828
- Ben!
- [Gasps]

126
00:09:57.897 --> 00:09:59.990
Hey. You all right?

127
00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:03.630
[Sighs]

128
00:10:03.703 --> 00:10:06.297
Don't worry. The, uh...

129
00:10:06.372 --> 00:10:08.363
kids are resilient.

130
00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:10.341
They're gonna be all right.

131
00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:12.400
- Yeah.
- [School bell ringing in distance]

132
00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:14.469
I'm late. I gotta go.

133
00:10:16.482 --> 00:10:18.848
- Deardra. Bill.
- Hey, Judy.

134
00:10:18.918 --> 00:10:21.512
Little man.
How y'all doing?

135
00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:23.817
Uh, would you mind
taking a look at Bill?

136
00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:25.823
- Sure. What's wrong?
- I don't know.

137
00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:29.554
He's just...
He's not right.

138
00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:32.928
[Air hissing]

139
00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:35.490
How are you feeling, Bill?

140
00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:37.934
Any pain or discomfort?

141
00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:41.372
Bill?

142
00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:44.273
She worries too much. I'm fine.

143
00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:46.368
Just a little tired.

144
00:10:46.445 --> 00:10:48.174
You got any plans this weekend?

145
00:10:50.016 --> 00:10:52.883
She worries too much. I'm fine.

146
00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:55.546
Just a little tired.

147
00:10:55.621 --> 00:10:57.851
His vitals are fine.

148
00:10:57.923 --> 00:11:01.518
But, you know, I've gotta see a patient
in Cedar Rapids on Monday.

149
00:11:01.594 --> 00:11:03.687
I wanna take Bill in to get a CT scan.

150
00:11:03.763 --> 00:11:05.060
- Monday?
- Yeah.

151
00:11:05.131 --> 00:11:08.225
Let's just make sure it's nothing serious.

152
00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.733
- Okay.
- Okay?

153
00:11:09.802 --> 00:11:11.531
You need me, you call me.

154
00:11:11.604 --> 00:11:12.935
Day or night.

155
00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:14.097
- Okay?
- Thanks, Judy.

156
00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:15.697
- [Taps hood]
- See you, Nicholas.

157
00:11:15.775 --> 00:11:18.141
- [Nicholas] Bye, Judy.
- Bye, Bill!

158
00:11:46.172 --> 00:11:49.164
[Heavy equipment whirring]

159
00:11:52.311 --> 00:11:53.744
[Whirring continues]

160
00:11:56.248 --> 00:11:58.580
What's Dad doing?

161
00:12:00.486 --> 00:12:02.647
Wait here, Nicholas.

162
00:12:36.722 --> 00:12:38.519
William!

163
00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:45.624
William?

164
00:12:53.405 --> 00:12:55.339
William, what are you doing?

165
00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:05.246
[Engine stops]

166
00:13:23.402 --> 00:13:24.733
William?

167
00:13:31.744 --> 00:13:33.678
William!

168
00:13:33.746 --> 00:13:36.340
- [Nicholas screaming]
- Oh, God.

169
00:13:36.415 --> 00:13:38.144
Nicholas!

170
00:13:44.723 --> 00:13:46.691
Nicholas?

171
00:13:49.762 --> 00:13:51.855
[Whimpering]

172
00:13:53.332 --> 00:13:55.357
- [Wood creaking]
- Nicholas.

173
00:13:59.205 --> 00:14:00.194
Nicholas!

174
00:14:04.443 --> 00:14:06.877
[Squeaking]

175
00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.814
[Gasps]

176
00:14:09.882 --> 00:14:11.440
- Nicholas, are you okay?
- Shh, shh.

177
00:14:14.987 --> 00:14:16.955
Nicholas, what happened?

178
00:14:18.557 --> 00:14:19.854
It's Dad.

179
00:14:19.959 --> 00:14:22.154
Wh-Where's Dad?

180
00:14:22.228 --> 00:14:24.128
What happened?

181
00:14:24.196 --> 00:14:25.686
Honey, please, talk to me.

182
00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:27.823
Please.

183
00:14:29.134 --> 00:14:31.125
He has a knife.

184
00:14:32.471 --> 00:14:34.405
- [Footsteps approaching]
- Oh, my God.

185
00:14:39.345 --> 00:14:40.812
Stay back.

186
00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.347
Stay right there.

187
00:14:42.414 --> 00:14:45.474
[Panting]

188
00:14:45.551 --> 00:14:47.951
[Footsteps continue]

189
00:15:08.941 --> 00:15:11.671
[Screams, whimpering]

190
00:15:20.853 --> 00:15:22.787
- [Rattling]
- William!

191
00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:25.247
William!

192
00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.022
[Match strikes]

193
00:15:35.567 --> 00:15:37.262
William!

194
00:15:38.971 --> 00:15:42.099
William, please, don't do this!

195
00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:46.404
William, please let us out!

196
00:15:51.884 --> 00:15:56.082
[Deardra shouting]

197
00:15:56.155 --> 00:16:00.148
- [Screaming]
- [Pounding]

198
00:16:00.225 --> 00:16:03.752
[Phone ringing]

199
00:16:03.829 --> 00:16:06.127
[Sighs]

200
00:16:06.198 --> 00:16:08.257
[Ringing continues]

201
00:16:10.035 --> 00:16:11.866
Hello.

202
00:16:11.937 --> 00:16:13.495
Mmm.

203
00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:17.504
I'm coming.

204
00:16:19.111 --> 00:16:20.840
What is it?

205
00:16:20.913 --> 00:16:22.039
[Siren wails]

206
00:16:22.114 --> 00:16:24.048
[Fireman]
Number 1, take the full pressure.

207
00:16:24.116 --> 00:16:26.346
All right, team.
Get me some power.

208
00:16:26.418 --> 00:16:28.352
- Oh, my God.
- The garage is lit up, too.

209
00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.854
- Deardra!
- Tom, they get out?

210
00:16:30.923 --> 00:16:33.892
Not Deardra and Nicholas.
Just Bill.

211
00:16:33.959 --> 00:16:36.757
- I need two men on that Engine 3 quarter, south side.
- On it.

212
00:16:36.829 --> 00:16:39.457
When we got here, there was
an empty gas can just sitting out front.

213
00:16:39.531 --> 00:16:42.432
- And Bill... Well, he was mowing the goddamn lawn.
- %% [humming]

214
00:16:42.501 --> 00:16:45.937
David, Deardra and Nicholas
were upstairs locked inside a closet.

215
00:16:46.005 --> 00:16:48.098
- Bill! Bill!
- %% [humming continues]

216
00:16:48.173 --> 00:16:50.004
Bill?

217
00:16:50.075 --> 00:16:52.543
What the hell happened here?

218
00:16:52.611 --> 00:16:54.875
[Firemen shouting]

219
00:16:54.947 --> 00:16:56.312
- Oh, my God.
- Judy.

220
00:16:56.382 --> 00:16:57.371
Oh, God.

221
00:16:57.449 --> 00:16:59.212
- Judy, come on.
- No.

222
00:16:59.284 --> 00:17:01.479
- What the fuck have you done?
- Judy, come on.

223
00:17:01.553 --> 00:17:03.453
- Oh! Oh, David!
- Shh.

224
00:17:03.522 --> 00:17:06.047
Oh, God!

225
00:17:06.125 --> 00:17:07.888
%% [humming continues]

226
00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:09.120
[Woman]
Deardra!

227
00:17:09.194 --> 00:17:12.129
- %% [whistling]
- Oh, my God!

228
00:17:12.197 --> 00:17:14.028
Deardra!

229
00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.239
[Bird calling]

230
00:17:39.925 --> 00:17:41.483
What the hell?

231
00:17:46.532 --> 00:17:48.523
What the hell?

232
00:17:52.004 --> 00:17:53.096
What you got?

233
00:17:57.042 --> 00:17:59.442
[Shouts]

234
00:17:59.511 --> 00:18:00.876
Shit!

235
00:18:00.946 --> 00:18:02.573
- Oh, my God.
- [Groans]

236
00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:07.177
Russ, you get in touch
with Sheriff Byrnes in Cedar Rapids?

237
00:18:10.189 --> 00:18:12.089
- Russ?
- Uh, yeah.

238
00:18:12.191 --> 00:18:14.523
State troopers are coming this afternoon
to pick him up for transfer.

239
00:18:14.593 --> 00:18:16.322
How long has he been playing statue?

240
00:18:16.395 --> 00:18:18.386
[David]
A couple hours now.

241
00:18:20.065 --> 00:18:22.260
The same look Rory gave me.

242
00:18:22.367 --> 00:18:24.699
The same goddamn look.

243
00:18:29.741 --> 00:18:30.730
[Phone ringing]

244
00:18:30.809 --> 00:18:33.039
[Scoffs]
Shit.

245
00:18:35.881 --> 00:18:37.314
[Russ]
Sheriff's Department.

246
00:18:38.951 --> 00:18:41.715
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Slow down. Slow down.

247
00:18:48.393 --> 00:18:50.827
[Jim] Been there at least a week
by the looks of things.

248
00:18:50.896 --> 00:18:53.956
I'll check to see
if there's any identification.

249
00:18:54.032 --> 00:18:56.125
- [Blows nose]
- Yeah.

250
00:18:56.201 --> 00:18:57.361
Do that.

251
00:18:59.938 --> 00:19:03.567
Boys, last I checked,
hunting season ended three months ago.

252
00:19:03.642 --> 00:19:05.803
We was just out taking in a little nature.

253
00:19:05.878 --> 00:19:08.369
- Fresh air is all.
- Guns away till fall.

254
00:19:08.447 --> 00:19:10.745
- Aw, come on, Sheriff.
- What, are you kidding me?

255
00:19:10.816 --> 00:19:13.376
- What's with this guy?
- Well, we got us a pilot.

256
00:19:13.452 --> 00:19:15.852
Where's the plane?

257
00:19:15.921 --> 00:19:18.355
You know, last week,
Travis Quinn was going around

258
00:19:18.423 --> 00:19:21.119
saying he heard something crash
out by Hautman Bog.

259
00:19:21.226 --> 00:19:24.195
- I didn't think nothing of it.
- On account of him being full of shit?

260
00:19:24.263 --> 00:19:26.197
As a general rule.

261
00:19:26.265 --> 00:19:29.723
- Well, maybe there's the exception.
- Maybe.

262
00:19:37.242 --> 00:19:39.608
[Russ]
You said it sounded like a plane, Trav?

263
00:19:39.678 --> 00:19:41.339
Sheriff, about the reward...

264
00:19:41.413 --> 00:19:43.677
Shit. Big plane? Little plane?
What? Come on now.

265
00:19:43.749 --> 00:19:45.683
If you can explain the difference
how those two sound,

266
00:19:45.751 --> 00:19:47.912
- I might be able to figure it out.
- You're full of shit.

267
00:19:47.986 --> 00:19:49.681
He's full of shit.

268
00:19:49.755 --> 00:19:52.349
People only ask for a reward
when there's something to find.

269
00:19:52.424 --> 00:19:53.857
Is it gonna be a big reward, Sheriff?

270
00:19:53.926 --> 00:19:55.359
Travis, you ask about that again,

271
00:19:55.427 --> 00:19:57.190
I'm gonna throw you
out of the fucking boat.

272
00:19:57.262 --> 00:19:58.524
You're not gonna shoot me?

273
00:20:01.166 --> 00:20:02.428
Travis.

274
00:20:03.335 --> 00:20:04.461
Yeah?

275
00:20:04.536 --> 00:20:06.265
Kill the engine.

276
00:20:09.441 --> 00:20:10.703
[Engine stops]

277
00:20:10.776 --> 00:20:13.370
It was a big plane, Russ.

278
00:20:13.445 --> 00:20:15.037
Why is that?

279
00:20:15.113 --> 00:20:17.343
'Cause we're right on top of it.

280
00:20:35.801 --> 00:20:38.463
[Radio chatter]

281
00:20:47.579 --> 00:20:50.571
Kevin, which way does
the water flow through town?

282
00:20:50.649 --> 00:20:52.344
Nice to see you, too, Dave.

283
00:20:52.417 --> 00:20:54.112
Waste water or drinking?

284
00:20:54.186 --> 00:20:56.416
- Drinking.
- Give me a second.

285
00:20:58.223 --> 00:21:00.157
A plane that size goes down...

286
00:21:00.225 --> 00:21:02.352
nothing in the paper,
nothing in the news.

287
00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:05.294
- Make any sense to you?
- It depends on what the payload is.

288
00:21:05.364 --> 00:21:07.264
Exactly what I'm thinking.

289
00:21:07.332 --> 00:21:09.493
Which is what?

290
00:21:09.568 --> 00:21:11.934
Hautman Bog...
What's that drain into?

291
00:21:12.004 --> 00:21:13.596
- Dwyer Creek.
- Which drains into?

292
00:21:13.672 --> 00:21:15.833
Black Pond. Oh, hey,
you remember monster catfish...

293
00:21:15.907 --> 00:21:19.172
Russell, where do you think
we get our drinking water from?

294
00:21:19.244 --> 00:21:22.372
Treated water comes in from the north,
breaks east-west.

295
00:21:22.447 --> 00:21:24.108
And what house does it get to first?

296
00:21:24.182 --> 00:21:26.776
Uh, let's see.

297
00:21:26.852 --> 00:21:28.251
Rory Hamill.

298
00:21:36.194 --> 00:21:40.324
You wanna shut off
the entire town's water supply on a hunch?

299
00:21:40.399 --> 00:21:43.960
Mayor, I've got three dead bodies
in the morgue in the last 48 hours.

300
00:21:44.036 --> 00:21:46.163
David, take a look around you.

301
00:21:46.238 --> 00:21:48.001
This is a farming community.

302
00:21:48.073 --> 00:21:50.007
It is springtime.
It is planting season.

303
00:21:50.075 --> 00:21:51.975
You turn off the water,
you're gonna kill the crops.

304
00:21:52.044 --> 00:21:55.639
You kill the crops, and you bankrupt
every family in Pierce County.

305
00:21:55.714 --> 00:21:58.740
And that is not based
on some, uh, hunch.

306
00:21:58.817 --> 00:22:00.250
That's a fact.

307
00:22:02.087 --> 00:22:04.578
Water stays on.

308
00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:19.998
Uh, Sheriff,

309
00:22:20.072 --> 00:22:21.664
I'm all for a little civil disobedience,

310
00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:24.766
but, um, I think this one
might cost you your job.

311
00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:29.547
You know what, Russ?

312
00:22:32.851 --> 00:22:35.342
That wouldn't be such a bad thing.

313
00:22:47.366 --> 00:22:48.993
What the fuck?

314
00:22:58.443 --> 00:23:00.673
Shh. Hang on a second.

315
00:23:04.783 --> 00:23:06.614
Well, is he dead?

316
00:23:09.221 --> 00:23:12.315
Well, if he is, he won't mind waiting.

317
00:23:14.726 --> 00:23:16.125
[Screaming]

318
00:23:16.194 --> 00:23:18.492
Oh! Jesus Christ!

319
00:23:21.233 --> 00:23:24.600
Did we or did we not request
a transfer for him this morning?

320
00:23:24.669 --> 00:23:25.658
Mm-hmm.

321
00:23:26.872 --> 00:23:29.670
- [Busy signal]
- [Dialing]

322
00:23:29.741 --> 00:23:31.470
God damn it.

323
00:23:35.013 --> 00:23:36.571
- [Busy signal]
- [Dialing]

324
00:23:36.648 --> 00:23:38.707
- Even better.
- [Receiver clatters]

325
00:23:38.784 --> 00:23:41.344
[Typing]

326
00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:44.321
- You know what?
- What?

327
00:23:45.757 --> 00:23:47.122
We're in trouble.

328
00:23:51.229 --> 00:23:53.789
[Beeping]

329
00:24:20.091 --> 00:24:21.854
Hello?

330
00:24:23.395 --> 00:24:26.228
%% [Woman singing]

331
00:24:26.298 --> 00:24:30.701
% % All things wise and wonderful% %

332
00:24:30.769 --> 00:24:33.897
% % And our Lord loves them all% %

333
00:24:33.972 --> 00:24:37.135
%% [singing continues]

334
00:24:37.209 --> 00:24:38.870
[Camera shutter clicking]

335
00:24:50.789 --> 00:24:52.620
[Tires screeching]

336
00:25:01.566 --> 00:25:04.262
[Clattering in distance]

337
00:25:05.837 --> 00:25:07.304
[Glass shatters]

338
00:25:16.481 --> 00:25:18.142
Jim?

339
00:25:24.756 --> 00:25:26.917
[Clattering in distance]

340
00:25:32.097 --> 00:25:33.792
Jim?

341
00:25:38.537 --> 00:25:40.437
[Dripping]

342
00:26:03.361 --> 00:26:05.454
[Clattering in distance]

343
00:26:05.530 --> 00:26:08.795
[Man groaning]

344
00:26:20.378 --> 00:26:22.141
[Muffled crying]

345
00:26:22.213 --> 00:26:23.805
Jesus Christ.

346
00:26:34.726 --> 00:26:36.318
Behind you.

347
00:26:44.736 --> 00:26:48.001
[Groaning]

348
00:26:56.214 --> 00:26:57.613
[Whirring]

349
00:26:57.682 --> 00:26:59.115
[Grunts]

350
00:27:07.025 --> 00:27:08.959
[Yelling]

351
00:27:23.975 --> 00:27:26.603
[Screaming]

352
00:27:54.639 --> 00:27:56.163
Christ Almighty.

353
00:28:03.515 --> 00:28:05.449
[Judy]
David, I'm not gonna do this.

354
00:28:05.517 --> 00:28:07.178
I can't go to my parents.

355
00:28:07.252 --> 00:28:09.277
- You have no idea...
- And neither do you.

356
00:28:09.354 --> 00:28:12.187
Look, whatever it is,
I can't just leave.

357
00:28:12.257 --> 00:28:14.225
- Are you gonna leave?
- I'm the sheriff.

358
00:28:14.292 --> 00:28:15.691
- I'm their doctor.
- Yeah, well,

359
00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:17.523
if it turns out what they need is penicillin,

360
00:28:17.595 --> 00:28:19.688
- I'll call you.
- [Drawer opens]

361
00:28:19.764 --> 00:28:20.856
David.

362
00:28:20.932 --> 00:28:21.956
What?

363
00:28:24.469 --> 00:28:25.458
What?

364
00:28:27.305 --> 00:28:28.897
There's somebody outside.

365
00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:23.991
David!

366
00:29:24.062 --> 00:29:25.689
David!

367
00:29:27.332 --> 00:29:28.959
- Get on the ground!
- [Soldiers shouting]

368
00:29:29.033 --> 00:29:30.591
This is secure.

369
00:29:30.668 --> 00:29:32.966
[Shouting continues]

370
00:29:33.037 --> 00:29:35.631
All right! Let's go, men! Move it!

371
00:29:35.707 --> 00:29:37.641
Come on. Let's go.
Keep it moving.

372
00:29:37.709 --> 00:29:40.109
[Radio chatter]

373
00:29:40.178 --> 00:29:42.043
[Man]
Sheriff, what's going on?

374
00:29:42.113 --> 00:29:44.274
- I don't know any more than you do.
- Keep moving, sir.

375
00:29:44.349 --> 00:29:45.475
Please take the first open seat.

376
00:29:45.550 --> 00:29:48.383
A funny thing happened
on the way to Cedar Rapids.

377
00:29:48.453 --> 00:29:50.819
Bastards spiked my tires.

378
00:29:50.889 --> 00:29:53.289
Who are these fuckers, man?

379
00:30:26.658 --> 00:30:30.287
[Radio chatter]

380
00:30:30.361 --> 00:30:32.591
Keep moving.
Everyone must exit the bus.

381
00:30:32.664 --> 00:30:33.926
Keep moving, please.

382
00:30:33.998 --> 00:30:35.863
- Let's go, let's go!
- [Equipment beeping]

383
00:30:35.934 --> 00:30:38.767
Stay in line, sir.
Keep up with the group, please.

384
00:30:38.837 --> 00:30:41.931
- [Man on P.A. System, indistinct]
- Please head into the tent.

385
00:30:42.006 --> 00:30:44.304
- There is no need for alarm.
- Inside, please.

386
00:30:44.375 --> 00:30:46.775
- Forward, please.
- [Mechanical humming]

387
00:30:46.845 --> 00:30:48.938
- Please keep moving into the tent.
- Please step forward.

388
00:30:49.013 --> 00:30:51.038
Let's go.
Keep moving, please.

389
00:30:51.115 --> 00:30:53.208
Hey, can one of you guys
tell me what's going on?

390
00:30:53.284 --> 00:30:56.447
- I'm sorry. You're gonna have to keep moving.
- Sir, come with me.

391
00:30:56.521 --> 00:30:57.545
- Let's go!
- No!

392
00:30:57.622 --> 00:30:59.112
- [David] Russell!
- Don't touch me!

393
00:30:59.190 --> 00:31:01.181
- Coming through!
- The temperature spiked.

394
00:31:01.259 --> 00:31:05.127
- [Child crying]
- [Woman yelling]

395
00:31:05.196 --> 00:31:07.630
- Ma'am...
- What are you people doing?

396
00:31:07.699 --> 00:31:09.360
Judy... Hey, don't touch me.

397
00:31:09.434 --> 00:31:11.402
- Hey!
- Both of you, out!

398
00:31:11.469 --> 00:31:13.937
Let's go.
Keep moving, please.

399
00:31:14.005 --> 00:31:16.405
- Go ahead. This way, please.
- [David] Judy, what does it mean?

400
00:31:16.474 --> 00:31:18.601
- They're checking for elevated temperatures.
- Clear.

401
00:31:18.676 --> 00:31:20.871
Farnum was bleeding from the nose.
So was Rory.

402
00:31:20.945 --> 00:31:22.378
Well, cerebral hemorrhaging...

403
00:31:22.447 --> 00:31:24.210
It's gotta be some kind of virus.

404
00:31:24.282 --> 00:31:26.375
- You gotta wait here.
- Look, I'm a sheriff.

405
00:31:26.451 --> 00:31:28.214
- She's a doctor. We know these people.
- Clear.

406
00:31:28.286 --> 00:31:31.221
Would you just tell us what's going on?
Maybe we can actually help you.

407
00:31:31.289 --> 00:31:33.723
- [Fast beeping]
- [Man shouting]

408
00:31:33.791 --> 00:31:35.554
- Take her in there!
- David!

409
00:31:35.627 --> 00:31:37.060
[Shouting continues]

410
00:31:37.128 --> 00:31:38.254
Go, go, go!

411
00:31:38.329 --> 00:31:41.560
David!
Get off me! Stop!

412
00:31:41.633 --> 00:31:45.296
David! Wait! Wait!

413
00:31:45.370 --> 00:31:47.065
[Soldier]
Stand back! Now!

414
00:31:47.138 --> 00:31:49.072
- Wait! Wait! Wait!
- Judy! Judy!

415
00:31:49.140 --> 00:31:50.300
Wait!

416
00:31:51.476 --> 00:31:53.774
David! David!

417
00:31:53.845 --> 00:31:55.676
- Judy!
- [Judy screams]

418
00:31:55.747 --> 00:31:56.736
[Groans]

419
00:31:56.814 --> 00:32:00.875
David! David! David!

420
00:32:02.820 --> 00:32:04.117
[Judy whispering]
Please.

421
00:32:04.188 --> 00:32:06.019
Please help me.

422
00:32:06.090 --> 00:32:08.320
Please. Please.

423
00:32:08.393 --> 00:32:11.021
[People shouting, screaming]

424
00:32:17.168 --> 00:32:20.262
Keep it moving.
Keep it moving.

425
00:32:20.338 --> 00:32:22.465
We got Trayberg scrubbed and ready.

426
00:32:22.540 --> 00:32:24.508
Let's go, let's go.

427
00:32:27.445 --> 00:32:29.379
Please. Please.

428
00:32:29.447 --> 00:32:31.540
Don't. Please. Don't.

429
00:32:33.584 --> 00:32:35.381
No.

430
00:32:35.453 --> 00:32:36.715
No.

431
00:32:36.788 --> 00:32:38.449
- No. Please.
- [Gas hissing]

432
00:32:38.523 --> 00:32:41.014
Please. I'm pregnant.

433
00:32:41.092 --> 00:32:42.719
Please! No!

434
00:32:42.794 --> 00:32:45.558
[Muffled shouting]

435
00:32:45.630 --> 00:32:47.120
[Muffled screaming]

436
00:32:47.198 --> 00:32:50.634
- [Brakes squealing]
- [Radio chatter]

437
00:32:53.938 --> 00:32:56.406
[People chattering]

438
00:33:09.253 --> 00:33:10.311
[Soldier]
Let's go!

439
00:33:10.388 --> 00:33:12.720
Franklin, open these doors!

440
00:33:13.891 --> 00:33:15.756
Quickly, people.
We're getting you outta here.

441
00:33:15.827 --> 00:33:17.658
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

442
00:33:17.729 --> 00:33:19.594
- Keep moving!
- Come on!

443
00:33:20.898 --> 00:33:23.958
[Chattering]

444
00:33:25.403 --> 00:33:26.995
Let's go, let's go.

445
00:33:27.071 --> 00:33:29.562
Extend your right arm,
please, sir. Let's go.

446
00:33:29.640 --> 00:33:32.165
You'll be given a card.
It looks like this.

447
00:33:32.243 --> 00:33:35.007
Do not lose it.

448
00:33:35.079 --> 00:33:36.410
[Beeps]

449
00:33:37.815 --> 00:33:39.840
Keep it moving.

450
00:33:46.524 --> 00:33:50.483
- [Coughing]
- [Laughing]

451
00:33:50.628 --> 00:33:53.529
[Man on radio] We have an inbound vehicle
coming in from the northern perimeter.

452
00:33:53.598 --> 00:33:55.793
Do you have clearance ID? Over.

453
00:33:58.669 --> 00:34:01.695
- [Alarm blaring]
- We have no ID.

454
00:34:01.773 --> 00:34:04.367
- [Alarm continues]
- [Radio chatter]

455
00:34:04.442 --> 00:34:06.103
- [Horn honking]
- [Gunfire]

456
00:34:06.177 --> 00:34:07.838
[Clamoring]

457
00:34:07.945 --> 00:34:10.209
We have gunfire!

458
00:34:10.281 --> 00:34:11.873
[soldiers shouting]

459
00:34:11.949 --> 00:34:15.009
- [Shouting continues]
- It's a civilian vehicle!

460
00:34:17.455 --> 00:34:19.389
- Behind you!
- Right there! Right there!

461
00:34:19.457 --> 00:34:20.947
[Cries out]

462
00:34:24.796 --> 00:34:27.287
[Clamoring]

463
00:34:32.136 --> 00:34:35.162
[Man shouting on radio]

464
00:34:37.308 --> 00:34:38.570
Keep moving.

465
00:34:38.643 --> 00:34:40.611
Kevin, where's Linda?

466
00:34:40.678 --> 00:34:43.408
- They took her. Judy?
- They took her, too.

467
00:34:43.481 --> 00:34:45.108
They took George and Francine

468
00:34:45.183 --> 00:34:46.582
and Winton Simon
and a whole mess of other people.

469
00:34:46.651 --> 00:34:49.279
- Jake! Jake! Jake!
- Mom!

470
00:34:49.353 --> 00:34:51.651
Let's go, people.
Keep moving. Keep moving.

471
00:34:51.722 --> 00:34:53.690
I'm going back.

472
00:34:53.758 --> 00:34:55.749
They got the whole town sealed off.

473
00:34:55.827 --> 00:34:57.692
Roadblocks on every highway.

474
00:34:57.762 --> 00:34:59.457
Tim Mitchell tried to run one.

475
00:34:59.530 --> 00:35:01.293
They shot him dead.
His entire family.

476
00:35:01.365 --> 00:35:02.798
Keep it moving.
Come up ahead.

477
00:35:02.867 --> 00:35:04.994
David, this here
might be your only chance.

478
00:35:05.069 --> 00:35:08.163
Don't lose it running off
on some fool's errand.

479
00:35:08.239 --> 00:35:10.764
Judy's a fool's errand?

480
00:35:10.842 --> 00:35:12.833
You know what I'm saying.

481
00:35:14.912 --> 00:35:16.812
I'll tell you what, Kev.

482
00:35:16.881 --> 00:35:18.872
Don't ask me why I can't leave
without my wife.

483
00:35:18.950 --> 00:35:20.577
I won't ask you why you can.

484
00:35:27.592 --> 00:35:30.686
[Soldier] We got a breach in the yard!
Got a breach in the yard!

485
00:35:30.761 --> 00:35:33.025
Move out! Move out!
Let's go! Evacuate!

486
00:35:33.097 --> 00:35:35.327
Come on!
Let's go! Let's go!

487
00:35:35.399 --> 00:35:37.458
The crazies have breached
the containment area!

488
00:35:37.535 --> 00:35:40.470
- The military's pulling out!
- We gotta get outta here!

489
00:35:40.538 --> 00:35:43.974
[Radio chatter]

490
00:35:44.041 --> 00:35:45.668
Come on! Go!
Get on board!

491
00:35:45.743 --> 00:35:47.643
- We're outta here!
- Move! Move! Move!

492
00:35:47.712 --> 00:35:51.011
- [People shouting]
- Take 'em out!

493
00:35:51.082 --> 00:35:54.711
On board! On board!

494
00:36:28.119 --> 00:36:29.586
[Door opens]

495
00:36:31.489 --> 00:36:32.922
[Running footsteps]

496
00:36:34.926 --> 00:36:36.188
Nice to see you, too, Chief.

497
00:36:36.260 --> 00:36:38.592
- [Vehicle approaching]
- Oh, shit.

498
00:36:47.805 --> 00:36:49.102
How'd you get out?

499
00:36:49.173 --> 00:36:50.401
Tom Ellis ran his pickup
through the fence.

500
00:36:50.474 --> 00:36:52.374
Fucking military started shooting.

501
00:36:52.443 --> 00:36:54.035
Townsfolk going nuts.

502
00:36:54.111 --> 00:36:57.046
Before you know it,
people are just running off into the fields.

503
00:36:57.114 --> 00:36:59.344
David, Judy was still inside.

504
00:36:59.417 --> 00:37:01.544
- I'm sorry.
- She's not sick.

505
00:37:01.619 --> 00:37:04.816
She's been running a fever all month.
Russ, she's pregnant.

506
00:37:04.889 --> 00:37:06.083
It's about time.

507
00:37:06.157 --> 00:37:08.125
I'm gonna go get her.

508
00:37:08.192 --> 00:37:10.956
Hoo-fucking-yah.
Let's go to the high school.

509
00:37:20.371 --> 00:37:23.135
- [Man laughing]
- [Grunting]

510
00:37:31.682 --> 00:37:32.944
[People coughing]

511
00:37:33.017 --> 00:37:36.077
Becca? Becca!

512
00:37:36.153 --> 00:37:38.053
Is that you?

513
00:37:39.223 --> 00:37:41.589
Oh, God. Honey...

514
00:37:41.659 --> 00:37:44.423
Honey, are you hurt?

515
00:37:44.495 --> 00:37:46.622
Is this really happening?

516
00:37:46.697 --> 00:37:50.326
It's gonna be all right.
We're gonna be okay.

517
00:37:50.401 --> 00:37:53.632
You don't really believe that, do you?

518
00:37:53.704 --> 00:37:57.162
[Metallic scraping in distance]

519
00:38:07.018 --> 00:38:10.647
[Scraping continues]

520
00:38:10.721 --> 00:38:13.189
Shh.

521
00:38:58.169 --> 00:38:59.659
[Woman muttering]

522
00:39:17.588 --> 00:39:19.579
[Screaming]

523
00:39:19.657 --> 00:39:21.284
[Grunting]

524
00:39:23.994 --> 00:39:25.291
[Gasps]

525
00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.867
[Metallic scraping]

526
00:39:32.937 --> 00:39:35.428
[Laughing]

527
00:39:45.683 --> 00:39:47.776
[Grunts]

528
00:39:47.852 --> 00:39:49.945
[Grunts]

529
00:39:51.455 --> 00:39:53.355
[Whimpers]

530
00:40:00.731 --> 00:40:02.358
[Whimpers]

531
00:40:05.970 --> 00:40:08.768
- [Metallic scraping]
- [Becca crying]

532
00:40:08.839 --> 00:40:10.272
Oh. Shh. Shh.

533
00:40:10.341 --> 00:40:13.640
Please, Principal Sandborn, please stop.

534
00:40:13.711 --> 00:40:15.576
Please, let me go.

535
00:40:15.646 --> 00:40:18.342
Please don't do this.

536
00:40:18.416 --> 00:40:19.974
No. Please don't do this.

537
00:40:20.050 --> 00:40:23.315
Please. No, no. Please.

538
00:40:23.387 --> 00:40:25.651
[Judy]
No!

539
00:40:35.666 --> 00:40:37.031
Oh, shit.

540
00:40:44.208 --> 00:40:46.199
- [Metallic scraping]
- What are you doing? Stop!

541
00:40:46.277 --> 00:40:48.268
No. Please. Please.

542
00:40:48.345 --> 00:40:51.280
- No! N...
- Just get out of here, please.

543
00:40:51.348 --> 00:40:54.442
- Stop. Please go. Don't.
- [Yelling]

544
00:40:54.518 --> 00:40:56.850
- Don't hurt her. Please, just go away.
- Please.

545
00:40:56.921 --> 00:40:58.286
Please.

546
00:40:58.355 --> 00:41:01.290
Please stop. Please stop.

547
00:41:01.358 --> 00:41:03.952
Stop. Leave her alone.

548
00:41:04.028 --> 00:41:05.655
- [Whimpering]
- Stop.

549
00:41:05.729 --> 00:41:08.664
- Please just get out of here. Please.
- [Shouts]

550
00:41:08.732 --> 00:41:10.461
No.
[Muttering]

551
00:41:10.534 --> 00:41:11.660
No.

552
00:41:11.735 --> 00:41:13.202
[Shouts]

553
00:41:13.270 --> 00:41:14.202
- No!
- [Gunshot]

554
00:41:14.271 --> 00:41:15.533
[Screaming]

555
00:41:15.606 --> 00:41:18.404
- [Grunts]
- Oh! Oh!

556
00:41:18.476 --> 00:41:21.741
Oh, God! Oh, David!

557
00:41:21.812 --> 00:41:24.508
David! Oh, God!

558
00:41:24.582 --> 00:41:26.550
- Are you okay?
- [Panting]

559
00:41:26.617 --> 00:41:29.279
No, not really.

560
00:41:31.055 --> 00:41:34.821
- Uh, Chief?
- We gotta get to Quik Phil's truck stop on 35.

561
00:41:34.892 --> 00:41:37.986
They're putting people on buses,
and they're getting them out of here.

562
00:41:39.163 --> 00:41:42.257
[Judy]
We're gonna go. Come on.

563
00:41:44.235 --> 00:41:47.329
- [Woman] Did Peter call?
- Shh.

564
00:41:49.073 --> 00:41:52.042
- Did Peter call?
- [Russell] That's gonna be me.

565
00:41:52.109 --> 00:41:55.203
Russell, we've got enough problems
without you inventing them.

566
00:41:55.279 --> 00:41:57.008
- That's easy for you to say.
- Did Peter call?

567
00:41:57.081 --> 00:41:58.605
You're at the end of the pot mine.

568
00:41:58.682 --> 00:42:00.274
I'm a half mile from the farm.

569
00:42:00.351 --> 00:42:01.375
- Who's the sheriff?
- What?

570
00:42:01.452 --> 00:42:03.386
Who's the sheriff of Pierce County?

571
00:42:03.454 --> 00:42:05.615
- You are.
- I am. Who's the deputy?

572
00:42:05.689 --> 00:42:07.020
- That would be me.
- You are.

573
00:42:07.091 --> 00:42:08.524
Deputy does what the sheriff tells him.

574
00:42:08.592 --> 00:42:11.891
That's the balance of power.
And I'm telling you,

575
00:42:11.962 --> 00:42:14.795
you're not getting sick,
you understand me?

576
00:42:15.966 --> 00:42:18.161
Did Peter call?

577
00:42:20.137 --> 00:42:22.264
Did Peter call?

578
00:42:23.274 --> 00:42:25.139
I hope you're right, Chief.

579
00:42:25.209 --> 00:42:28.610
- [Door opens, closes]
- I'm not world leader, but I had plans.

580
00:42:28.679 --> 00:42:30.146
Did Peter call?

581
00:42:30.214 --> 00:42:31.806
Come on.

582
00:42:33.617 --> 00:42:36.017
[Alarm ringing in distance]

583
00:42:45.296 --> 00:42:47.457
Let's go.

584
00:42:57.041 --> 00:43:00.238
[Banging in distance]

585
00:43:04.481 --> 00:43:07.314
[Banging continues]

586
00:43:15.359 --> 00:43:17.350
I'll check the truck.

587
00:43:19.430 --> 00:43:20.761
Fuck.

588
00:43:22.733 --> 00:43:25.668
Aw, shit!
It's booted.

589
00:43:29.173 --> 00:43:31.164
- They all are.
- I'll check those cars.

590
00:43:40.584 --> 00:43:43.451
It's not booted.

591
00:43:47.524 --> 00:43:49.389
Whoa, whoa.

592
00:43:50.394 --> 00:43:52.453
Russell,

593
00:43:52.529 --> 00:43:54.019
get out of the truck.

594
00:43:54.098 --> 00:43:56.532
- Just give me a second.
- [Gunshot]

595
00:43:56.600 --> 00:43:58.124
[David]
Oh, Jesus.

596
00:43:58.202 --> 00:44:00.966
Go. Run. Go on.

597
00:44:01.038 --> 00:44:03.006
Go, go, go, go,
go, go, go, go.

598
00:44:03.073 --> 00:44:04.597
Get down, get down, get down.

599
00:44:10.080 --> 00:44:12.310
[Man]
Come on, boys.

600
00:44:12.383 --> 00:44:14.044
Come on! Get him!

601
00:44:16.053 --> 00:44:18.351
Come on! Yeah!

602
00:44:18.422 --> 00:44:19.980
Whoo!

603
00:44:20.057 --> 00:44:21.422
Oh, yeah!

604
00:44:23.093 --> 00:44:24.993
- Whoo!
- Run, little man!

605
00:44:25.062 --> 00:44:26.757
Run!

606
00:44:26.830 --> 00:44:28.559
- Get him!
- Whoo!

607
00:44:28.632 --> 00:44:30.827
[Gunshot]

608
00:44:30.901 --> 00:44:33.233
- Nice shot. Nice shot.
- Oh, yeah!

609
00:44:33.303 --> 00:44:34.998
Huh? Nice shot.

610
00:44:35.072 --> 00:44:37.563
- Oh, yeah! Oh, yeah!
- Nice shot, huh?

611
00:44:37.641 --> 00:44:39.404
Whoo!

612
00:44:42.980 --> 00:44:45.210
Come on. Get him.

613
00:44:45.282 --> 00:44:48.183
Hey, straight through the heart!

614
00:44:48.252 --> 00:44:50.550
- Uh-huh!
- Yeah!

615
00:44:50.621 --> 00:44:52.179
- [Glass shatters]
- Shit.

616
00:44:52.256 --> 00:44:53.382
- Come on.
- Huh?

617
00:44:53.457 --> 00:44:55.391
Hey, he's gonna dress up real nice.

618
00:44:55.459 --> 00:44:58.587
Come on, boy.
[Laughs]

619
00:45:00.998 --> 00:45:02.989
Come on.
Get him up on there.

620
00:45:04.334 --> 00:45:07.360
[Men chattering, laughing]

621
00:45:17.715 --> 00:45:19.376
- Good shot, man.
- [Laughing]

622
00:45:19.450 --> 00:45:21.941
I knew I was okay about that shot.

623
00:45:23.120 --> 00:45:25.145
[Tires screeching]

624
00:45:28.892 --> 00:45:29.950
[Gunshot]

625
00:45:32.162 --> 00:45:33.459
[Gunshot]

626
00:45:42.639 --> 00:45:45.369
It's a hell of a walk to Quik Phil's.

627
00:45:47.044 --> 00:45:48.978
I got the old cruiser on blocks.

628
00:45:49.046 --> 00:45:51.071
That piece of shit still works?

629
00:45:51.148 --> 00:45:52.581
Yeah.

630
00:45:52.649 --> 00:45:55.117
I guess you can't boot
a car without wheels.

631
00:45:55.185 --> 00:45:57.085
It's seven miles to my place.

632
00:45:57.154 --> 00:45:58.917
It's five if we cut through
the McGregor farm.

633
00:45:58.989 --> 00:46:01.423
Another 20 to Quik Phil's from there.

634
00:46:02.493 --> 00:46:04.290
- I'm fine.
- Good.

635
00:46:04.361 --> 00:46:05.350
Let's go.

636
00:46:12.436 --> 00:46:14.495
[Judy]
They took my blood.

637
00:46:17.674 --> 00:46:20.837
Ran at least one test that I saw.

638
00:46:22.846 --> 00:46:25.610
What if the reason they didn't let me go
is because I have it?

639
00:46:25.682 --> 00:46:28.617
You're pregnant.
That's why you have a fever.

640
00:46:28.685 --> 00:46:32.280
David, you can't know that for sure.

641
00:46:32.356 --> 00:46:35.086
I can, and I do.

642
00:46:36.527 --> 00:46:39.553
If you're sick, I'm sick.
We drank from the same tap.

643
00:46:39.630 --> 00:46:42.622
And I'm not sick.
None of us are.

644
00:46:47.437 --> 00:46:49.371
We are gonna get through this.

645
00:46:56.213 --> 00:46:57.840
What the fuck?

646
00:46:57.915 --> 00:47:00.679
Scotty McGregor.
It's her boyfriend.

647
00:47:00.751 --> 00:47:01.911
Russell, stop her.

648
00:47:01.985 --> 00:47:02.974
- Yeah, I got it.
- David...

649
00:47:03.053 --> 00:47:05.248
We don't have time for this.

650
00:47:05.322 --> 00:47:07.381
You had time for me.

651
00:47:13.263 --> 00:47:15.231
[Whispers]
Okay, let's go.

652
00:47:18.468 --> 00:47:21.164
[Russell]
It looks deserted.

653
00:47:21.238 --> 00:47:22.569
[Becca]
Scotty?

654
00:47:25.642 --> 00:47:27.075
- Scotty?
- Get back!

655
00:47:27.144 --> 00:47:29.738
- Drop the fucking gun, Scotty.
- I will blow your head off.

656
00:47:29.813 --> 00:47:32.179
- Scotty, it's me.
- Stay here.

657
00:47:32.249 --> 00:47:36.185
Scotty, don't be an asshole.
We're fine.

658
00:47:38.822 --> 00:47:40.187
Scotty.

659
00:47:40.257 --> 00:47:42.191
[Russell]
Scotty, put the gun down.

660
00:47:42.259 --> 00:47:43.692
Put it down.

661
00:47:43.760 --> 00:47:45.421
Scotty.

662
00:47:55.939 --> 00:47:57.531
Sorry.

663
00:47:57.608 --> 00:47:59.200
[Sighs]

664
00:47:59.276 --> 00:48:01.267
Had to be sure.

665
00:48:01.345 --> 00:48:05.475
Yeah, well, that's
a two-way street there, Scotty.

666
00:48:08.118 --> 00:48:11.212
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

667
00:48:11.288 --> 00:48:12.983
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

668
00:48:13.056 --> 00:48:15.081
- Scotty, where's your mom?
- Back at the house.

669
00:48:15.158 --> 00:48:17.126
We were just getting some supplies
before we started walking.

670
00:48:17.194 --> 00:48:19.719
The sheriff's got a car.
You two can come with us.

671
00:48:19.796 --> 00:48:22.458
- Are you okay?
- Better than you guys.

672
00:48:22.532 --> 00:48:25.330
- How's your mom?
- Be quiet.

673
00:48:25.402 --> 00:48:28.166
- Get in the barn.
- Go, go, go, go, go.

674
00:48:34.378 --> 00:48:36.505
[Radio chatter]

675
00:48:57.668 --> 00:49:00.432
[Vehicle approaching]

676
00:49:00.504 --> 00:49:01.994
Russ.

677
00:49:05.175 --> 00:49:07.666
[Radio chatter]

678
00:49:10.280 --> 00:49:12.805
- [Soldier] We have one civilian coming out.
- [Woman] What are you doing?

679
00:49:12.883 --> 00:49:15.215
- [Man] Ma'am, please.
- [Woman] Stop! Stop!

680
00:49:15.285 --> 00:49:16.582
[Man]
We need you downstairs.

681
00:49:16.653 --> 00:49:18.314
- Everything's gonna be okay.
- Wait.

682
00:49:18.388 --> 00:49:20.982
- We just need to process you.
- [Sobbing] Oh, no.

683
00:49:21.058 --> 00:49:22.787
- Please!
- Okay, I got an adult male.

684
00:49:22.859 --> 00:49:24.656
- [Woman yelling]
- I just need you...

685
00:49:24.728 --> 00:49:26.286
- It'll just take a second, ma'am.
- [Thermometer beeping]

686
00:49:26.363 --> 00:49:28.092
[Soldier]
Too late.

687
00:49:28.165 --> 00:49:31.157
[Clamoring]

688
00:49:31.234 --> 00:49:33.065
[Soldier]
Hold it right there!

689
00:49:33.136 --> 00:49:36.105
- [Clamoring continues]
- [Gunshot]

690
00:49:36.173 --> 00:49:38.107
[Gasps]

691
00:49:38.175 --> 00:49:40.803
[Woman]
Scotty!

692
00:49:40.877 --> 00:49:42.242
[Gunshot]

693
00:49:42.312 --> 00:49:43.404
[Gasps]

694
00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:45.243
[Radio chatter]

695
00:49:45.315 --> 00:49:47.180
Okay, light them up.

696
00:49:57.494 --> 00:49:59.758
Okay, let's go! Split it up!

697
00:49:59.830 --> 00:50:02.094
I want a complete sweep of the area!

698
00:50:02.165 --> 00:50:03.928
Take my gun.
Close the back of the barn.

699
00:50:04.001 --> 00:50:07.027
[Soldier]
Move, move, move!

700
00:50:08.739 --> 00:50:11.139
[Cow lowing]

701
00:50:11.208 --> 00:50:13.335
[Radio chatter continues]

702
00:50:27.891 --> 00:50:29.882
[Lowing continues]

703
00:50:36.033 --> 00:50:38.024
Don't kill me, please.
Don't kill me.

704
00:50:38.101 --> 00:50:39.125
Oh, fuck.

705
00:50:39.202 --> 00:50:42.365
How could you do it?
How could you...

706
00:50:42.439 --> 00:50:44.373
- Becca...
- You make a sound louder than this,

707
00:50:44.441 --> 00:50:46.136
and I'll kill you, you understand?

708
00:50:46.209 --> 00:50:47.972
- What the hell was that?
- Orders, sir.

709
00:50:48.045 --> 00:50:49.808
- Who, asshole?
- Whoever gives them... I don't know.

710
00:50:49.880 --> 00:50:51.643
- Bullshit!
- What the fuck is going on here?

711
00:50:51.715 --> 00:50:54.047
All's they said is that there'd been
some sort of accident.

712
00:50:54.117 --> 00:50:56.813
My whole unit got flown in.
We didn't even know what state we was in

713
00:50:56.887 --> 00:51:00.050
till we seen the license plates.

714
00:51:00.123 --> 00:51:01.750
[Radio chatter]

715
00:51:04.895 --> 00:51:08.695
Am I gonna die without my mask on?

716
00:51:08.765 --> 00:51:10.892
Is that what they told you...

717
00:51:10.967 --> 00:51:12.901
If you took your mask off,
you were gonna die?

718
00:51:12.969 --> 00:51:16.132
They just said to keep it on.

719
00:51:17.140 --> 00:51:19.074
Look, um,

720
00:51:19.142 --> 00:51:21.838
I know I don't deserve
any favors from you people,

721
00:51:21.912 --> 00:51:24.904
but if you let me go,
I swear to God I won't say nothing.

722
00:51:24.981 --> 00:51:27.745
I didn't sign up
to shoot unarmed civilians.

723
00:51:29.152 --> 00:51:31.177
- I'll just leave, okay?
- Sit down.

724
00:51:31.254 --> 00:51:33.017
- Put the gun down, Russ.
- Chief...

725
00:51:35.325 --> 00:51:37.691
I'm a sheriff.
That's my deputy.

726
00:51:37.761 --> 00:51:40.457
Look, my wife's a doctor.
She's pregnant.

727
00:51:40.530 --> 00:51:42.896
- Becca here is not even 18.
- [Russ] When he blabs, they'll find us.

728
00:51:42.966 --> 00:51:45.025
If we don't let him go,
they'll find us for sure.

729
00:51:45.135 --> 00:51:48.263
And besides,
he's not gonna blab.

730
00:51:49.506 --> 00:51:51.133
No, sir.

731
00:51:56.780 --> 00:51:58.680
[Breathing heavily]

732
00:52:00.851 --> 00:52:02.876
You gotta give it to him, Russ.

733
00:52:02.953 --> 00:52:03.942
Shit.

734
00:52:04.020 --> 00:52:06.716
I'm sorry about your folks' town.

735
00:52:06.790 --> 00:52:09.156
- Hey, one up!
- Don't shoot! Don't shoot!

736
00:52:09.226 --> 00:52:11.126
Any crazies back there, Babcock?

737
00:52:14.297 --> 00:52:15.821
Babcock?

738
00:52:16.867 --> 00:52:18.562
No. We're all clear.

739
00:52:18.635 --> 00:52:20.933
Good. Military's pulling
back to the perimeter.

740
00:52:21.004 --> 00:52:22.972
Let's go. Come on.

741
00:52:25.242 --> 00:52:27.176
Barn's clear!

742
00:52:27.244 --> 00:52:29.439
- We're secure back there!
- All right, then.

743
00:52:29.513 --> 00:52:32.004
Mount up!
We're moving out!

744
00:52:32.082 --> 00:52:35.074
[Wind chimes jingling]

745
00:52:48.565 --> 00:52:51.056
[Becca crying]

746
00:52:51.134 --> 00:52:54.194
[Judy]
If what that soldier said is true,

747
00:52:54.271 --> 00:52:56.762
this disease has gone airborne.

748
00:52:59.910 --> 00:53:02.640
[David]
We just have to keep going.

749
00:54:01.638 --> 00:54:04.004
Uh, we'll go and get
the car up and running.

750
00:54:04.074 --> 00:54:06.304
- Come on.
- Go.

751
00:54:09.679 --> 00:54:12.239
Hey.

752
00:54:12.315 --> 00:54:14.010
Hey, hey, hey.

753
00:54:14.084 --> 00:54:16.245
[Muttering]

754
00:54:23.360 --> 00:54:25.351
It's perfect.

755
00:54:27.264 --> 00:54:30.461
It's a perfect, beautiful morning,

756
00:54:30.533 --> 00:54:32.467
and this is our home.

757
00:54:32.535 --> 00:54:34.469
This is where we were
gonna raise our baby.

758
00:54:34.537 --> 00:54:36.698
We can still do all those things.

759
00:54:36.773 --> 00:54:38.104
Hmm?

760
00:54:39.542 --> 00:54:42.033
Everyone we know...

761
00:54:42.112 --> 00:54:43.943
is dead.

762
00:54:46.549 --> 00:54:51.009
This town is dead,
and it's not coming back.

763
00:54:52.589 --> 00:54:55.023
It's never coming back.

764
00:55:02.732 --> 00:55:03.994
[Whistles]
Fuck, yeah.

765
00:55:04.067 --> 00:55:06.297
See if you can find a toolbox.

766
00:55:06.369 --> 00:55:07.859
Okay.

767
00:55:40.603 --> 00:55:43.128
This was gonna be your room.

768
00:56:01.791 --> 00:56:04.316
%% [chimes]

769
00:56:24.814 --> 00:56:27.442
%% [continues]

770
00:56:31.287 --> 00:56:33.152
Judy.

771
00:56:36.960 --> 00:56:38.222
Look, I know this is hard,

772
00:56:38.294 --> 00:56:41.058
- but we've gotta keep moving.
- [Muffled shouting]

773
00:56:47.637 --> 00:56:49.468
[Straining]

774
00:56:49.539 --> 00:56:51.302
%% [continues]

775
00:56:59.482 --> 00:57:00.915
[Muffled screaming]

776
00:57:00.984 --> 00:57:02.815
[Groaning]

777
00:57:12.695 --> 00:57:14.424
This is the gun that killed your father.

778
00:57:19.269 --> 00:57:20.258
[Gunshot]

779
00:57:20.336 --> 00:57:22.133
[Yelling]

780
00:57:22.205 --> 00:57:24.673
Baby.

781
00:57:24.741 --> 00:57:27.505
[David]
Peggy... Peggy, no. Not Judy.

782
00:57:27.577 --> 00:57:28.942
[David grunting]

783
00:57:29.012 --> 00:57:30.604
No. No, no, no.

784
00:57:30.680 --> 00:57:32.773
I shot him.
I did. I shot him.

785
00:57:32.849 --> 00:57:34.441
Yes.

786
00:57:34.517 --> 00:57:36.280
- Peggy, I shot him.
- [Muffled screaming]

787
00:57:36.352 --> 00:57:38.320
Look at me, you crazy bitch!

788
00:57:38.388 --> 00:57:41.516
That's it.
I fucking shot him!

789
00:57:41.591 --> 00:57:43.456
I did it!

790
00:57:43.526 --> 00:57:45.858
He walked on that field
with a loaded shotgun!

791
00:57:45.929 --> 00:57:48.193
And I'm glad I did!

792
00:57:48.264 --> 00:57:50.061
They should give me a fucking medal!
[Cries out]

793
00:57:50.133 --> 00:57:52.294
I finally killed the town drunk!

794
00:57:53.303 --> 00:57:54.463
[Muffled screaming]

795
00:57:58.575 --> 00:57:59.837
[Gagging]

796
00:57:59.909 --> 00:58:01.240
[Grunts]

797
00:58:13.289 --> 00:58:16.383
[Grunting]

798
00:58:21.598 --> 00:58:22.656
[Muffled screaming]

799
00:58:22.732 --> 00:58:23.721
[Gunshot]

800
00:58:25.635 --> 00:58:26.727
Oh!

801
00:58:26.803 --> 00:58:28.566
[Judy screaming]

802
00:58:34.744 --> 00:58:36.974
[Sobbing]

803
00:58:43.653 --> 00:58:45.712
- Oh, God.
- We're okay.

804
00:58:45.788 --> 00:58:47.847
- [Judy] Baby!
- Oh, my God.

805
00:58:49.259 --> 00:58:51.193
Let me see your hand.

806
00:58:51.261 --> 00:58:53.525
Give me the Betadine.

807
00:58:56.833 --> 00:58:58.892
Yep, that's it. Here.

808
00:58:58.968 --> 00:59:00.026
Shit.

809
00:59:08.111 --> 00:59:09.100
[Gurgles]

810
00:59:11.281 --> 00:59:13.476
[Screaming]

811
00:59:13.550 --> 00:59:16.383
Russell. Russell!

812
00:59:16.452 --> 00:59:18.352
Just making sure.

813
00:59:34.504 --> 00:59:36.495
He's sick, David.

814
00:59:38.474 --> 00:59:40.408
You don't know that.

815
00:59:40.476 --> 00:59:41.636
- You saw what he did.
- Hey, guys.

816
00:59:41.711 --> 00:59:44.145
Come on. We gotta go.

817
00:59:47.083 --> 00:59:49.017
He saved our lives.

818
00:59:49.085 --> 00:59:51.076
That's what I saw.

819
01:00:19.849 --> 01:00:21.783
[Coughing]

820
01:00:21.851 --> 01:00:23.409
[Clears throat]

821
01:00:28.024 --> 01:00:30.185
[Clears throat]

822
01:00:30.259 --> 01:00:31.658
[Coughing]

823
01:00:31.728 --> 01:00:34.288
[Coughing continues]

824
01:00:38.534 --> 01:00:40.161
Hey, you feeling okay?

825
01:00:40.236 --> 01:00:42.568
- She's fine.
- Well, I'm just saying, if she's getting sick,

826
01:00:42.639 --> 01:00:45.233
- we don't wanna be in the fucking car with her.
- Russell, she's fine.

827
01:00:45.308 --> 01:00:46.798
I'm not sick.

828
01:00:46.876 --> 01:00:49.811
You wouldn't know,
'cause that'd be the sickness

829
01:00:49.879 --> 01:00:52.040
- messing with your mind.
- [David] Okay. Russell, that's enough.

830
01:00:52.115 --> 01:00:54.811
Don't lose your head.

831
01:00:54.884 --> 01:00:57.318
What do you mean by that?

832
01:00:57.387 --> 01:00:59.378
I mean, don't lose your head.

833
01:00:59.455 --> 01:01:01.013
What do you mean by that, Chief?

834
01:01:01.090 --> 01:01:02.887
I mean...

835
01:01:02.959 --> 01:01:04.824
She's fine.

836
01:01:06.562 --> 01:01:07.893
Now, just...

837
01:01:11.100 --> 01:01:13.091
Fuck!

838
01:01:14.570 --> 01:01:17.505
- Did he see us?
- I don't know.

839
01:01:17.573 --> 01:01:21.339
- David, honey...
- Aw, shit.

840
01:01:21.411 --> 01:01:23.106
Guys, it's turning around.

841
01:01:23.179 --> 01:01:24.339
- It's coming back for us!
- Shit! Let's go!

842
01:01:24.414 --> 01:01:27.406
We gotta get out of here!

843
01:01:27.483 --> 01:01:30.281
- [Russell] Go! Chief, let's go!
- The helicopter's coming!

844
01:01:43.599 --> 01:01:45.931
[Helicopter approaching]

845
01:01:48.771 --> 01:01:51.205
[Helicopter departing]

846
01:01:53.109 --> 01:01:54.940
- We can't stay on the highway.
- No.

847
01:01:55.011 --> 01:01:56.603
There's gotta be another road we can take.

848
01:01:56.679 --> 01:01:59.239
- What road? Tell me?
- I don't know. There's gotta be something.

849
01:01:59.315 --> 01:02:01.215
- What road can they not see? Tell me.
- What?

850
01:02:01.284 --> 01:02:03.218
What road can they not see?

851
01:02:03.286 --> 01:02:04.878
What magic road can they not see?

852
01:02:04.954 --> 01:02:07.252
Tell me, and I'll fucking go.

853
01:02:07.323 --> 01:02:10.451
David, I'm just trying to help.

854
01:02:12.862 --> 01:02:15.592
I'm sorry.

855
01:02:15.665 --> 01:02:17.223
[Screams]

856
01:02:17.300 --> 01:02:19.768
- I saw someone.
- Move. Where?

857
01:02:19.836 --> 01:02:22.737
He was back there.
I know I saw someone.

858
01:02:22.805 --> 01:02:24.739
Uh...

859
01:02:24.807 --> 01:02:28.140
- Oh, fuck.
- Shit.

860
01:02:29.679 --> 01:02:31.078
What the fuck?

861
01:02:32.915 --> 01:02:34.246
[Judy]
David, get us outta here.

862
01:02:35.985 --> 01:02:39.284
- [Screams]
- Oh, shit.

863
01:02:39.355 --> 01:02:41.915
- Start the car.
- [Engine cranking]

864
01:02:41.991 --> 01:02:43.083
[Russell]
Come on, Chief.

865
01:02:43.159 --> 01:02:44.592
[Cranking continues]

866
01:02:44.660 --> 01:02:46.423
[Russell] Let's go. Come on.
Get us outta here.

867
01:02:46.496 --> 01:02:50.592
[Cranking continues]

868
01:02:50.666 --> 01:02:51.758
Let's go! Let's go!

869
01:02:51.834 --> 01:02:53.131
[Shouts]

870
01:02:53.202 --> 01:02:54.999
Come on!

871
01:02:57.340 --> 01:02:58.671
[Engine cranking continues]

872
01:03:02.078 --> 01:03:03.670
- Come on!
- [Engine starts]

873
01:03:03.746 --> 01:03:05.441
- Let's go!
- All right!

874
01:03:05.515 --> 01:03:07.608
- [Engine revving]
- Come on!

875
01:03:07.683 --> 01:03:10.015
[Russell]
Come on! Let's go!

876
01:03:10.086 --> 01:03:12.111
- Why aren't we moving?
- Why the fuck aren't we moving, Chief?

877
01:03:12.188 --> 01:03:14.850
- 'Cause I can't get any fucking traction.
- Go! Go!

878
01:03:14.924 --> 01:03:17.119
Fuck! Let's go!
Get us outta here! Come on!

879
01:03:17.193 --> 01:03:19.286
[Becca screaming]

880
01:03:19.362 --> 01:03:21.125
I don't wanna die like this!

881
01:03:21.197 --> 01:03:23.062
[Russell]
What the fuck was that?

882
01:03:26.536 --> 01:03:28.970
- There! There! Right there!
- Motherfucker!

883
01:03:29.038 --> 01:03:30.027
- Russell... Russ...
- There!

884
01:03:30.106 --> 01:03:31.095
Oh, shit!

885
01:03:31.174 --> 01:03:32.163
[Gunshots]
Motherfucker!

886
01:03:32.241 --> 01:03:34.209
[Women screaming]

887
01:03:34.277 --> 01:03:35.608
- Russell!
- [Gunshot]

888
01:03:35.678 --> 01:03:38.112
- Oh, fuck!
- Russell!

889
01:03:38.181 --> 01:03:39.512
I saw movement!

890
01:03:39.582 --> 01:03:42.142
- Everything is fucking moving!
- [Thud]

891
01:03:52.528 --> 01:03:54.894
[Screaming]

892
01:03:54.964 --> 01:03:57.159
[Yelling]

893
01:04:01.771 --> 01:04:04.035
[Screaming continues]

894
01:04:06.876 --> 01:04:08.173
[Snarling]

895
01:04:21.858 --> 01:04:23.849
Go! Come on! Come on!

896
01:04:31.200 --> 01:04:32.633
[Screaming]

897
01:04:34.537 --> 01:04:36.903
- Stop the fucking car!
- Stop! Stop! Stop!

898
01:04:36.973 --> 01:04:38.804
- Stop the car!
- [Brakes screeching]

899
01:04:38.875 --> 01:04:40.467
- Stop!
- Judy!

900
01:04:41.978 --> 01:04:44.913
Shit! David!

901
01:04:44.981 --> 01:04:47.415
Help me here!
Help me!

902
01:04:47.483 --> 01:04:51.078
Oh, God, please.
You're okay.

903
01:04:51.153 --> 01:04:55.112
Becca! Becca! Becca!

904
01:05:03.799 --> 01:05:05.289
[Whispers]
Oh, no.

905
01:05:11.207 --> 01:05:12.799
Becca.

906
01:05:15.244 --> 01:05:16.302
[Crying]

907
01:05:18.681 --> 01:05:20.308
No.

908
01:05:21.651 --> 01:05:22.982
Becca.

909
01:05:41.704 --> 01:05:43.331
[Sobbing]

910
01:05:46.008 --> 01:05:48.533
[Chuckling]

911
01:05:52.848 --> 01:05:54.440
[Mutters]

912
01:06:20.576 --> 01:06:22.635
[Russell]
That's my truck.

913
01:06:22.712 --> 01:06:25.044
Fuckers spiked my tires.

914
01:06:37.093 --> 01:06:38.822
Shit.

915
01:06:44.633 --> 01:06:47.727
- [Ignition clicks]
- [Sighs]

916
01:06:50.406 --> 01:06:52.033
God damn it!

917
01:06:52.108 --> 01:06:54.838
We need water.

918
01:06:54.910 --> 01:06:56.343
I know.

919
01:06:56.412 --> 01:06:59.404
[Russell]
Guys, car coming!

920
01:07:09.258 --> 01:07:11.089
Stay here.

921
01:07:11.160 --> 01:07:13.060
David, what are you doing?

922
01:07:13.129 --> 01:07:15.359
We're taking this car.

923
01:07:29.178 --> 01:07:31.544
- Motherfucker!
- Russ!

924
01:07:31.614 --> 01:07:33.377
What are you... No!

925
01:07:34.483 --> 01:07:36.144
- [Tires screeching]
- Whoo!

926
01:07:59.375 --> 01:08:03.072
Welcome to Pierce County,
friendliest place on earth, asshole.

927
01:08:03.145 --> 01:08:05.079
- Russ, I wanna talk to him.
- [Coughs]

928
01:08:06.715 --> 01:08:08.615
Okay.

929
01:08:08.684 --> 01:08:10.914
Who the fuck do you think you are?

930
01:08:10.986 --> 01:08:14.251
- I'm the guy standing between you and a bullet.
- [Groans]

931
01:08:14.323 --> 01:08:17.190
Now, what was on that plane?

932
01:08:17.259 --> 01:08:20.194
What was on that goddamn plane?

933
01:08:20.262 --> 01:08:21.695
Trixie.

934
01:08:21.764 --> 01:08:24.130
Rhabdoveridae prototype.

935
01:08:24.200 --> 01:08:26.259
A... A fucking biological weapon.
- It was headed

936
01:08:26.335 --> 01:08:29.099
- to an incinerator in Texas.
- Whoa. What is this?

937
01:08:29.171 --> 01:08:31.765
You're telling me that you guys
engineered this crap?

938
01:08:31.841 --> 01:08:34.435
It's designed to destabilize a population.

939
01:08:34.510 --> 01:08:36.603
In this case, the wrong one.

940
01:08:36.679 --> 01:08:38.203
Look, fella, we lost a plane.

941
01:08:38.280 --> 01:08:40.407
What do you want me to say?

942
01:08:43.185 --> 01:08:45.949
How about, "Sorry for destroying
your whole goddamn town"?

943
01:08:46.021 --> 01:08:48.455
- What would you have preferred, a global pandemic?
- Wait. Wait.

944
01:08:48.524 --> 01:08:51.220
Take it up with the pilot.
I came here to help.

945
01:08:51.293 --> 01:08:53.158
Help who? Help us?

946
01:08:53.229 --> 01:08:55.288
What... What is the incubation period?

947
01:08:55.364 --> 01:08:57.298
48 hours.

948
01:08:57.366 --> 01:08:59.800
After that, you're either dead
or you don't have it.

949
01:08:59.869 --> 01:09:02.997
Fine. It's day three,
and we're still talking.

950
01:09:03.072 --> 01:09:04.835
So you are gonna help us.

951
01:09:04.907 --> 01:09:06.033
[Gunshot]

952
01:09:07.443 --> 01:09:08.876
What the fuck!

953
01:09:08.944 --> 01:09:10.536
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no!
- Oh, my God!

954
01:09:10.613 --> 01:09:12.513
What the fuck is the matter with you?

955
01:09:12.581 --> 01:09:14.640
I said that I wanted to talk to him!

956
01:09:16.218 --> 01:09:17.480
You talked.

957
01:09:47.016 --> 01:09:48.005
Shit.

958
01:09:53.422 --> 01:09:55.447
I'm gonna need that back.

959
01:09:55.524 --> 01:09:56.957
[David]
I'll carry it for a while.

960
01:09:57.026 --> 01:09:59.586
- You've been carrying it the whole time.
- Oh, no. Really.

961
01:09:59.662 --> 01:10:01.289
I got it.

962
01:10:01.363 --> 01:10:03.729
You sure?

963
01:10:03.799 --> 01:10:05.130
Yeah.

964
01:10:10.039 --> 01:10:11.199
[Gun cocks]

965
01:10:18.514 --> 01:10:20.539
Russell, we're on your side.

966
01:10:20.616 --> 01:10:22.914
My side? Shit.
I didn't even know there were sides.

967
01:10:22.985 --> 01:10:25.044
- There's not. I'm just...
- Shut up the fuck up!

968
01:10:25.120 --> 01:10:27.281
- Tell her to shut up, or I'll kill her, too.
- Russell, no!

969
01:10:27.356 --> 01:10:29.586
- Judy, stop talking.
- Okay.

970
01:10:29.658 --> 01:10:31.592
Let him think about what he's doing.

971
01:10:31.660 --> 01:10:33.457
Uh-huh.

972
01:10:35.531 --> 01:10:39.467
One, two,

973
01:10:39.535 --> 01:10:41.332
three.

974
01:10:43.572 --> 01:10:46.564
That's how many times
I've saved your life.

975
01:10:48.477 --> 01:10:49.774
Go on.

976
01:10:49.845 --> 01:10:51.779
Walk out where I can see you.

977
01:10:51.847 --> 01:10:52.836
Move!

978
01:11:18.540 --> 01:11:19.905
Fucking heavy.

979
01:11:24.413 --> 01:11:26.313
[Clicks]

980
01:11:26.382 --> 01:11:28.213
Move!

981
01:11:28.284 --> 01:11:29.774
Move!

982
01:11:39.528 --> 01:11:42.725
- Fuck it. I'm gonna confront him.
- No, David. Don't. Please.

983
01:11:42.798 --> 01:11:46.495
If we don't make it to that truck stop,
we're dead anyway.

984
01:11:46.568 --> 01:11:49.036
- Don't, David. Don't.
- Back off!

985
01:11:49.104 --> 01:11:51.629
- I wanna talk to you.
- I will fucking shoot you where you stand.

986
01:11:51.707 --> 01:11:53.538
- I just wanna talk.
- David, stop.

987
01:11:53.609 --> 01:11:55.304
You better listen to me.

988
01:11:55.377 --> 01:11:56.810
- David.
- Put the gun down.

989
01:11:56.879 --> 01:11:59.575
- Final warning, Chief.
- Put it down.

990
01:11:59.648 --> 01:12:02.674
Please? Just put it down.

991
01:12:02.751 --> 01:12:05.151
I just wanna talk.

992
01:12:05.220 --> 01:12:08.815
You and me, man to man.

993
01:12:08.891 --> 01:12:10.552
Come on.

994
01:12:11.927 --> 01:12:13.758
- Shit.
- Okay.

995
01:12:13.829 --> 01:12:15.558
Here's the deal.

996
01:12:16.665 --> 01:12:18.724
Fuck!

997
01:12:31.780 --> 01:12:33.111
Hey.

998
01:12:34.750 --> 01:12:37.742
You remember that monster catfish
I caught last summer?

999
01:12:37.820 --> 01:12:39.788
What'd he weigh, you reckon?

1000
01:12:42.291 --> 01:12:45.522
35, 40 pounds.

1001
01:12:45.594 --> 01:12:47.186
Shit.

1002
01:12:47.262 --> 01:12:50.254
- It was a big son of a bitch.
- [Chuckles]

1003
01:13:01.877 --> 01:13:03.845
I'm not right, am I?

1004
01:13:16.125 --> 01:13:17.786
Can I walk with you guys?

1005
01:13:19.795 --> 01:13:22.389
Just a little while longer?

1006
01:13:24.333 --> 01:13:26.301
Please?

1007
01:13:49.391 --> 01:13:51.689
[Radio chatter]

1008
01:13:54.062 --> 01:13:56.053
[Radio chatter continues]

1009
01:13:59.701 --> 01:14:01.965
Shit.

1010
01:14:02.037 --> 01:14:05.473
If you cut through there,
you can make it to the highway on the other side.

1011
01:14:05.541 --> 01:14:08.533
- They'll see us.
- Nah, they'll be focusing on me.

1012
01:14:09.711 --> 01:14:12.646
Deputy does what
the sheriff tells him, right?

1013
01:14:12.714 --> 01:14:14.204
You're the sheriff.

1014
01:14:15.717 --> 01:14:17.810
Come on, Chief.

1015
01:14:17.886 --> 01:14:19.478
I'm done.

1016
01:14:19.555 --> 01:14:21.921
I'm gonna die here no matter what.

1017
01:14:21.990 --> 01:14:24.356
So let it mean something.

1018
01:14:24.426 --> 01:14:28.123
Let it mean that you two made it.
Give me that.

1019
01:14:48.917 --> 01:14:50.817
Hoo-fucking-yah.

1020
01:14:52.821 --> 01:14:55.051
[Soldier on radio]
We got an inbound!

1021
01:14:55.123 --> 01:14:57.023
- Hey!
- [Soldier on P.A.] Attention!

1022
01:14:57.092 --> 01:15:00.186
- You have entered a military operation.
- Hey! Hey!

1023
01:15:00.262 --> 01:15:02.127
- Please identify yourself.
- [Yelling]

1024
01:15:02.197 --> 01:15:03.858
My name's Deputy Russell Crank,

1025
01:15:03.932 --> 01:15:05.866
the Pierce County Sheriff's Department.

1026
01:15:05.934 --> 01:15:08.698
- Keep your hands in the air and walk slowly.
- It's okay. I'm not sick.

1027
01:15:08.770 --> 01:15:10.101
Make no sudden movements

1028
01:15:10.172 --> 01:15:11.867
- or you will be fired upon.
- Oh, shit.

1029
01:15:11.940 --> 01:15:14.238
We are a live-fire operation.

1030
01:15:14.309 --> 01:15:16.072
Get out from behind the vehicle.

1031
01:15:16.144 --> 01:15:19.272
You are in breach of
a Level 4 military operation.

1032
01:15:19.348 --> 01:15:22.010
[Radio chatter]

1033
01:15:25.654 --> 01:15:28.987
Reveal yourself,
or we will open fire.

1034
01:15:31.593 --> 01:15:34.494
- Proceed slowly with your hands in the air.
- It's okay.

1035
01:15:34.563 --> 01:15:36.190
It's okay.

1036
01:15:36.265 --> 01:15:38.995
Now stop there
and get down on the ground.

1037
01:15:39.067 --> 01:15:42.002
Stop and get down on the ground!

1038
01:15:42.070 --> 01:15:44.402
Get down on the ground now!

1039
01:15:44.473 --> 01:15:47.909
[soldiers shouting]

1040
01:15:47.976 --> 01:15:51.275
- He's down!
- Man down! Cease fire!

1041
01:15:51.346 --> 01:15:53.439
Fireteam Bravo, move up.

1042
01:15:53.515 --> 01:15:55.346
Alpha Team, stand by!

1043
01:15:55.417 --> 01:15:57.248
Let's go, let's go!

1044
01:15:59.955 --> 01:16:01.252
- [Gasping]
- Approach with caution.

1045
01:16:01.323 --> 01:16:03.689
Movement in tight.
He's still breathing!

1046
01:16:03.759 --> 01:16:06.353
Secure that weapon!

1047
01:16:06.428 --> 01:16:09.261
- Stay on him.
- [Gasping continues]

1048
01:16:10.999 --> 01:16:14.025
Fuck you for what you did.

1049
01:16:18.540 --> 01:16:19.871
[Gunshot in distance]

1050
01:16:26.248 --> 01:16:30.241
[Woman's voice on speaker]
Hey! Get an 18-Wheeler Dog

1051
01:16:30.319 --> 01:16:32.583
only at Quik Phil's.

1052
01:16:32.654 --> 01:16:35.748
Football fans,
show your support this off-season

1053
01:16:35.824 --> 01:16:39.260
with our University of Iowa
Hawkeyes Snack Pack.

1054
01:16:39.328 --> 01:16:42.422
One jar of hot sauce and one jar of salsa

1055
01:16:42.497 --> 01:16:44.727
in a collectible Iowa Hawkeyes helmet.

1056
01:16:44.800 --> 01:16:47.394
Available while supplies last

1057
01:16:47.469 --> 01:16:50.563
only at Quik Phil's.

1058
01:16:50.639 --> 01:16:52.903
It was Grand Central last night.

1059
01:16:52.975 --> 01:16:57.173
Nothing satisfies hunger
better than a Quik Phil's Mega-burger.

1060
01:16:57.245 --> 01:16:59.179
Take it to go or eat it here

1061
01:16:59.247 --> 01:17:02.808
- in one of our panoramic dining areas.
- Wait here.

1062
01:17:15.330 --> 01:17:17.230
Hello?

1063
01:17:44.092 --> 01:17:47.027
[Flies buzzing]

1064
01:18:12.954 --> 01:18:15.252
Judy?

1065
01:18:15.323 --> 01:18:19.282
Judy! Judy!

1066
01:18:24.132 --> 01:18:26.726
Judy, you all right?

1067
01:18:45.353 --> 01:18:47.480
[Whispers]
Ohh.

1068
01:19:02.003 --> 01:19:05.131
They exterminated everyone,
not just the sick.

1069
01:19:05.207 --> 01:19:07.607
- Look, there's a rig we can take.
- What's the point?

1070
01:19:07.676 --> 01:19:08.768
If we get out of here,

1071
01:19:08.844 --> 01:19:10.175
- they're gonna kill us, too.
- No.

1072
01:19:10.245 --> 01:19:12.543
- If we get to Cedar Rapids...
- David, can you just stop it?

1073
01:19:12.614 --> 01:19:15.344
- If we get to Cedar Rapids...
- Can you stop pretending

1074
01:19:15.417 --> 01:19:17.681
everything is gonna be okay?

1075
01:19:17.753 --> 01:19:19.345
All right.

1076
01:19:20.422 --> 01:19:22.219
For Christ sakes.

1077
01:19:28.930 --> 01:19:31.194
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1078
01:19:39.608 --> 01:19:40.973
You wanna give up?

1079
01:19:42.911 --> 01:19:44.469
You wanna sit here and die?

1080
01:19:44.546 --> 01:19:45.979
Tell me,

1081
01:19:46.047 --> 01:19:49.539
and I will sit here and die with you.

1082
01:20:14.843 --> 01:20:16.674
You gonna go get that truck?

1083
01:21:25.347 --> 01:21:27.577
[Man on radio]
Blackbird 2, this is T.O.C.

1084
01:21:27.649 --> 01:21:30.948
We are approaching T minus ten minutes.
Confirm status.

1085
01:21:31.019 --> 01:21:33.647
[Man #2]
This is Blackbird 2...

1086
01:21:51.339 --> 01:21:52.806
[Man #1]
All units, this is T.O.C.

1087
01:21:52.874 --> 01:21:54.808
Be advised we are at ready status.

1088
01:21:54.876 --> 01:21:57.367
Proceed to countdown.

1089
01:21:57.445 --> 01:21:59.640
[Woman]
Countdown procedure initiated.

1090
01:21:59.714 --> 01:22:02.444
We are at T minus ten minutes.

1091
01:22:02.517 --> 01:22:04.348
[Man]
All right. Blackbird 2 is in the air...

1092
01:22:09.524 --> 01:22:10.718
Truck!

1093
01:23:00.976 --> 01:23:02.409
[Screams]

1094
01:23:05.947 --> 01:23:07.437
[Gasps]

1095
01:23:33.475 --> 01:23:36.273
Oh, shit. Oh, shit.

1096
01:23:39.147 --> 01:23:41.138
[Footsteps approaching]

1097
01:23:55.363 --> 01:23:56.421
[Muttering]

1098
01:24:11.846 --> 01:24:14.542
[Clinking]

1099
01:24:14.616 --> 01:24:15.776
[Clinking stops]

1100
01:24:17.285 --> 01:24:20.846
[Footsteps]

1101
01:25:13.741 --> 01:25:16.539
[Metallic scraping]

1102
01:25:27.856 --> 01:25:30.450
[Muffled screaming]

1103
01:25:38.800 --> 01:25:40.768
[Screaming]

1104
01:25:43.238 --> 01:25:44.364
Honey, it's fine.

1105
01:25:44.439 --> 01:25:45.872
It's okay.

1106
01:25:45.940 --> 01:25:47.874
Oh, shit.

1107
01:25:53.047 --> 01:25:54.207
Oh, fuck.

1108
01:26:00.288 --> 01:26:03.655
David, honey,
how's it going there?

1109
01:26:03.725 --> 01:26:05.659
We're gonna get there.

1110
01:26:05.727 --> 01:26:10.164
Oh, shit. Baby, come on.
Come on. Come on.

1111
01:26:11.266 --> 01:26:12.255
David.

1112
01:26:12.333 --> 01:26:15.598
[Huffs]
God damn it!

1113
01:26:15.670 --> 01:26:17.729
David, come on.

1114
01:26:17.805 --> 01:26:19.773
- Hurry up.
- God damn it.

1115
01:26:19.841 --> 01:26:22.002
[Huffs]

1116
01:26:22.076 --> 01:26:24.101
I'm sorry. It's okay.

1117
01:26:24.179 --> 01:26:26.511
They've gotta be in here somewhere,
David. Come on.

1118
01:26:26.581 --> 01:26:28.742
- Just keep looking.
- Oh, fuck me. Just...

1119
01:26:28.816 --> 01:26:31.011
Jesus, David.
What are you doing?

1120
01:26:33.521 --> 01:26:34.818
Come on, baby. Come on.

1121
01:26:37.091 --> 01:26:38.217
David!

1122
01:26:38.293 --> 01:26:41.729
David! Quick! Come on!

1123
01:26:41.796 --> 01:26:43.127
[Growling]

1124
01:26:43.198 --> 01:26:44.426
[Screams]

1125
01:26:46.367 --> 01:26:48.597
David!

1126
01:27:08.990 --> 01:27:11.220
[Bones cracking]

1127
01:27:18.233 --> 01:27:20.793
[Blows landing]

1128
01:27:27.575 --> 01:27:28.701
[Gun cocks]

1129
01:27:45.493 --> 01:27:46.585
[David shouting]

1130
01:27:50.498 --> 01:27:51.863
[Snarling]

1131
01:28:01.676 --> 01:28:02.734
[Screaming]

1132
01:28:15.390 --> 01:28:18.291
[Panting]

1133
01:28:18.359 --> 01:28:19.587
[Sighs]

1134
01:28:22.230 --> 01:28:25.131
Let's get the fuck out of here, huh?

1135
01:28:25.199 --> 01:28:26.860
[Engine starts]

1136
01:28:44.886 --> 01:28:47.480
The smallest, straightest road
to Cedar Rapids.

1137
01:28:47.555 --> 01:28:49.386
Yeah. Perfect.

1138
01:28:54.128 --> 01:28:55.755
[Man on radio]
35, 34,

1139
01:28:55.830 --> 01:28:57.855
[Woman on radio]
61... Disengage.

1140
01:28:57.932 --> 01:28:59.832
- What happens when it gets to zero?
- [Man] 31,

1141
01:28:59.901 --> 01:29:03.337
- 30, 29, 28,
- [Woman] We are T minus 30 seconds and counting.

1142
01:29:03.404 --> 01:29:05.497
27, 26,

1143
01:29:05.573 --> 01:29:08.337
- 25, 24...
- Faster.

1144
01:29:11.245 --> 01:29:15.079
- 22, 21, 20,
- T minus 20 seconds. T.D.S. Is active.

1145
01:29:15.149 --> 01:29:18.175
- 19, 18, 17,
- You see anything?

1146
01:29:18.252 --> 01:29:20.846
- No.
- 16...

1147
01:29:20.922 --> 01:29:22.514
[engine revving]

1148
01:29:22.590 --> 01:29:24.683
14, 13,

1149
01:29:24.759 --> 01:29:27.387
- 12, 11,
- Auto sequence start.

1150
01:29:27.462 --> 01:29:30.863
- We are T minus ten seconds.
- 10, 9,

1151
01:29:30.932 --> 01:29:32.092
8...

1152
01:29:33.534 --> 01:29:37.197
- 6, 5, 4,
- Trigger engaged.

1153
01:29:37.271 --> 01:29:41.207
3, 2, 1.

1154
01:29:49.217 --> 01:29:50.582
[David]
Anything?

1155
01:29:50.651 --> 01:29:52.278
No.

1156
01:29:58.493 --> 01:30:03.089
[Explosion]

1157
01:30:03.164 --> 01:30:04.995
[Rumbling]

1158
01:30:09.337 --> 01:30:11.805
- Oh, my God.
- Oh!

1159
01:30:13.408 --> 01:30:15.399
[Rumbling intensifies]

1160
01:30:18.646 --> 01:30:19.908
- Get down!
- [Screams]

1161
01:30:34.762 --> 01:30:35.990
[Both shouting]

1162
01:30:39.100 --> 01:30:40.499
[Screams]

1163
01:31:06.527 --> 01:31:08.017
[Groans]

1164
01:31:12.066 --> 01:31:14.034
Hey, come on.

1165
01:31:15.069 --> 01:31:17.594
Come here. Come here.

1166
01:31:18.906 --> 01:31:20.635
[Groans]

1167
01:31:25.713 --> 01:31:27.578
Here.

1168
01:31:27.648 --> 01:31:29.309
Come on. Here.

1169
01:31:29.383 --> 01:31:30.611
[Groans]

1170
01:31:31.619 --> 01:31:35.055
- You okay?
- Yeah. I'm okay.

1171
01:31:35.122 --> 01:31:36.987
Yeah?

1172
01:31:37.992 --> 01:31:40.893
Come on. Come on.

1173
01:31:42.263 --> 01:31:43.753
Huh?

1174
01:31:47.235 --> 01:31:48.759
Yeah.

1175
01:32:29.544 --> 01:32:30.875
Ow.

1176
01:32:30.945 --> 01:32:32.435
Oh. Sorry, honey.

1177
01:33:04.011 --> 01:33:05.740
[Radio chatter]

1178
01:33:18.593 --> 01:33:21.585
.

1179
